<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="AMO" style="id">EN_ULT en_English_ltr Tue Jan 12 2021 12:09:22 GMT-0600 (Central Standard Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Amos
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Amos
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Amos
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Amo
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Amos

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="AMO 1"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 1:1"/>The words of Amos, who was among the sheepbreeders from Tekoa, which he saw concerning Israel in the days of Uzziah, the king of Judah, and in the days of Jeroboam son of Joash, the king of Israel, two years to the face of the earthquake.

<verse eid="AMO 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 1:2"/>And he said,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Yahweh roars from Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from Jerusalem he gives his voice,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the pastures of the shepherds mourn,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the head of Carmel dries up.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 1:3"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Damascus,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their threshing the Gilead
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the threshing sledges of iron.
<verse eid="AMO 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 1:4"/>And I will send a fire into the house of Hazael,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour the citadels of Ben Hadad.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 1:5"/>And I will break the bar of Damascus,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will cut off the seated {one} from the Valley of Aven
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one grasping the scepter from Beth Eden,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the people of Aram will go into exile to Kir,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">says Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 1:6"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Gaza,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their taking into exile a complete exile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to hand {them} over to Edom.
<verse eid="AMO 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 1:7"/>And I will send a fire on the wall of Gaza,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour her citadels.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 1:8"/>And I will cut off the seated {one} from Ashdod,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one grasping the scepter from Ashkelon,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will turn back my hand against Ekron,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the remnant of the Philistines will perish,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">says my Lord Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 1:9"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Tyre,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their handing over a complete exile to Edom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they did not remember the covenant of brothers.
<verse eid="AMO 1:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 1:10"/>And I will send a fire on the wall of Tyre,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour her citadels.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 1:11"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Edom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of his pursuing his brother with the sword,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he destroyed his compassions,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and his nose tore perpetually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his fury, he kept it continually.
<verse eid="AMO 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 1:12"/>And I will send a fire on Teman,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour the citadels of Bozrah.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:12"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 1:13"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of the sons of Ammon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their ripping open the pregnant women of the Gilead,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to enlarge their border.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 1:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 1:14"/>And I will kindle a fire in the wall of Rabbah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour her citadels,
</para>
  <para style="q1">with a shout in the day of battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a tempest in the day of the whirlwind.
<verse eid="AMO 1:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 1:15"/>And their king will go into the exile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he and his officials together,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">says Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 1:15"/><verse eid="AMO 1:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="AMO 2"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 2:1"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Moab,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of his burning the bones of the king of Edom
</para>
  <para style="q2">to lime.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 2:2"/>And I will send a fire into Moab,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour the citadels of Kerioth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Moab will die in an uproar,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a war cry, with the sound of the shofar.
<verse eid="AMO 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 2:3"/>And I will cut off the judge from her midst,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of her officials I will kill with him,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">says Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 2:4"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their rejecting the law of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they did not keep his statutes,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their lies led them astray,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which their fathers walked after them.
<verse eid="AMO 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 2:5"/>And I will send a fire into Judah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will devour the citadels of Jerusalem.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 2:6"/>Thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“For three transgressions of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for four, I will not turn it back,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because of their selling the righteous for silver,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the needy in exchange for a pair of sandals,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 2:7"/>the ones trampling on the head of the poor to the dust of the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they turn aside the way of the afflicted,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and a man and his father go to the girl,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to profane the name of my holiness.
<verse eid="AMO 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 2:8"/>And on garments taken in pledge they stretch out beside every altar,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the wine of the fined {ones} they drink in the house of their God.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 2:9"/>But I, I destroyed the Amorite from their faces,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who like the height of cedars {was} his height,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he {was} strong as the oaks,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I destroyed his fruit from above
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his roots from beneath.
<verse eid="AMO 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 2:10"/>And I, I brought you up from the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I led you in the wilderness forty years,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to possess the land of the Amorite.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 2:11"/>And I raised up from your sons as prophets,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from your young men as Nazirites.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Is it not even so, sons of Israel?”—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="AMO 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 2:12"/>“But you made the Nazirites drink wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the prophets you commanded, saying, ‘You shall not prophesy!’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 2:13"/>Behold, I am pressing down in your place,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as the cart presses down, the one that is full of sheaves for it.
<verse eid="AMO 2:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 2:14"/>And retreat will perish from the swift,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the strong will not strengthen his power,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the mighty will not save his life,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 2:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 2:15"/>and the one grasping the bow will not stand,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the swift on his feet will not save {himself},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one riding the horse will not save his life.
<verse eid="AMO 2:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="AMO 2:16"/>And the strong of his heart among the mighty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">naked he will flee in that day”—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 2:16"/><verse eid="AMO 2:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="AMO 3"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 3:1"/>Hear this word that Yahweh has spoken against you, sons of Israel, against all of the family that I brought up from the land of Egypt, saying,
<verse eid="AMO 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 3:2"/>“Only you have I known
</para>
  <para style="q2">from all of the families of the ground.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Therefore I will visit upon you
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of your iniquities.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 3:3"/>Will two walk together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">unless they have agreed?
<verse eid="AMO 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 3:4"/>Will a lion roar in the forest
</para>
  <para style="q2">when there is no prey for him?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Will a young lion give his voice from his den,
</para>
  <para style="q2">unless he has caught {something}?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 3:5"/>Will a bird fall into a snare {on} the ground
</para>
  <para style="q2">when there is no trap for it?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Will a snare spring up from the ground,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when capturing, it will not capture?
<verse eid="AMO 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 3:6"/>Or a shofar is blown in a city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the people do not tremble?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Or disaster happens in a city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh has not done {it}?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 3:7"/>For the Lord Yahweh will not do a thing
</para>
  <para style="q2">unless he has revealed his secret counsel to his servants the prophets.
<verse eid="AMO 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 3:8"/>The lion has roared;
</para>
  <para style="q2">who will not fear?
</para>
  <para style="q1">The Lord Yahweh has spoken;
</para>
  <para style="q2">who will not prophesy?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 3:9"/>Cause {people} to hear on the citadels in Ashdod,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the citadels in the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and say, ‘Be gathered on the mountains of Samaria,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and see the great uproars in her midst,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the oppressed within her.’
<verse eid="AMO 3:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 3:10"/>And they do not know to do right”—the declaration of Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q2">“those storing up violence and destruction in their citadels.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 3:11"/>Therefore, thus says the Lord Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“An adversary—and around the land!
</para>
  <para style="q2">And he will bring down from you your strength,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your citadels will be plundered.”

<verse eid="AMO 3:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 3:12"/>Thus says Yahweh:
</para>
  <para style="q1">“As the shepherd rescues from the mouth of the lion
</para>
  <para style="q2">two legs or a piece of an ear,
</para>
  <para style="q1">thus will the sons of Israel be rescued, the ones dwelling in Samaria,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with a side of a bed and with a cover of a couch.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 3:13"/>Hear, and testify against the house of Jacob”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh, the God of Armies—
<verse eid="AMO 3:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 3:14"/>“for in the day of my visiting the transgressions of Israel upon him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will also visit upon the altars of Bethel,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the horns of the altar will be cut off,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will fall to the ground.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 3:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 3:15"/>And I will strike the winter house with the summer house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the houses of ivory will perish,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and great houses will come to an end”—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 3:15"/><verse eid="AMO 3:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="AMO 4"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 4:1"/>Listen to this word, cows of Bashan,
</para>
  <para style="q1">who are in the mountain of Samaria,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones oppressing the poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones crushing the needy,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the ones saying to their masters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Bring, and let us drink.”
<verse eid="AMO 4:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 4:2"/>The Lord Yahweh has sworn by his holiness
</para>
  <para style="q1">that, behold, the days are coming upon you
</para>
  <para style="q2">when he will lift you up with hooks,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the last of you with hooks of fishery.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 4:3"/>And {through} the breaches you will go out, a woman in front of her,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you will throw {yourselves} out toward Harmon
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 4:4"/>Go to Bethel and transgress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to Gilgal and multiply to transgress,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and bring your sacrifices in the morning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">your tithes every three days.
<verse eid="AMO 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 4:5"/>And make a thank offering smoke from what is leavened,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and call out freewill offerings; make {people} hear!
</para>
  <para style="q1">For thus you have loved, sons of Israel
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 4:6"/>And even I, I gave to you cleanness of teeth in all your cities,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and lack of bread in all your places,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet you did not return as far as me
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="AMO 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 4:7"/>And also I, I withheld from you the rain
</para>
  <para style="q2">with still three months to the harvest.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I made it rain on one city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on one city I did not make it rain;
</para>
  <para style="q1">one portion was rained on,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a portion which it did not rain on it dried up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 4:8"/>And two–three cities staggered to one city to drink water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they were not satisfied,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet you did not return as far as me
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="AMO 4:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 4:9"/>I struck you with blight and with mildew;
</para>
  <para style="q1">the multitude of your gardens and your vineyards and your fig trees and your olive trees
</para>
  <para style="q2">the locust devoured,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet you did not return as far as me
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 4:10"/>I sent among you a plague in the way of Egypt;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I killed your young men with the sword, along with the captivity of your horses,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I made the stench of your camp come up, and into your nostrils,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet you did not return as far as me
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.
<verse eid="AMO 4:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 4:11"/>I overthrew among you as God overthrew Sodom and Gomorrah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you were like a firebrand snatched from a burning,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yet you did not return as far as me
</para>
  <para style="q2">—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 4:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 4:12"/>Therefore, thus I will do to you, Israel;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for the reason that I will do this to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">prepare to meet your God, Israel!
<verse eid="AMO 4:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 4:13"/>For behold, the {one} forming the mountains and creating the wind,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and declaring to man what {is} his thought,
</para>
  <para style="q1">making dawn darkness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and treading on the high places of the earth—
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, God of Armies, {is} his name.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 4:13"/><verse eid="AMO 4:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="AMO 5"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 5:1"/>Hear this word that I am lifting up over you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a lamentation, house of Israel:
<verse eid="AMO 5:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 5:2"/>She has fallen; she will not repeat to rise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the virgin Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q1">She is forsaken on her land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is no one raising her up.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 5:3"/>For thus says the Lord Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“The city going out a thousand will leave a hundred remaining,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the one going out a hundred will leave ten remaining
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the house of Israel.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 5:4"/>For thus says Yahweh to the house of Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Seek me and live,
<verse eid="AMO 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 5:5"/>and do not seek Bethel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not go to Gilgal,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not cross over to Beersheba;
</para>
  <para style="q1">for Gilgal, going into exile, will go into exile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Bethel will become iniquity.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:5"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 5:6"/>Seek Yahweh and live,
</para>
  <para style="q1">lest he break out like fire {in} the house of Joseph,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it consumes, and there is no extinguisher for Bethel,
<verse eid="AMO 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 5:7"/>the {ones} turning justice into wormwood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they cast righteousness to the ground!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 5:8"/>The maker of the Pleiades and Orion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">turning deep darkness into morning;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he darkens day into night;
</para>
  <para style="q1">calling for the waters of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he pours them out on the face of the earth—
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is his name—
<verse eid="AMO 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 5:9"/>the one making destruction flash against the strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and destruction comes against the fortress.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 5:10"/>They hate the reprover in the gate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they abhor the one speaking blamelessly.
<verse eid="AMO 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 5:11"/>Therefore, because of your trampling on the poor
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you take a tax of grain from him:
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have built houses of hewn stone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you will not dwell in them;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have planted vineyards of desire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you will not drink their wine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 5:12"/>For I know your transgressions {are} many,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your sins {are} mighty—
</para>
  <para style="q1">oppressors of the righteous, takers of a bribe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they turn aside the needy in the gate.
<verse eid="AMO 5:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 5:13"/>Therefore the prudent will be still in that time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for it {is} an evil time.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 5:14"/>Seek good, and not evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you may live;
</para>
  <para style="q1">and thus may Yahweh, God of Armies, be with you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as you have said.
<verse eid="AMO 5:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 5:15"/>Hate evil, and love good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and establish justice in the gate;
</para>
  <para style="q1">perhaps Yahweh, God of Armies, will be gracious
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the remnant of Joseph.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:15"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="AMO 5:16"/>Therefore thus says Yahweh, God of Armies, the Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“In all plazas {there will be} wailing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in all streets they will say, ‘Alas! Alas!’
</para>
  <para style="q1">And they will call the farmer to mourning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wailing to those knowing a lament.
<verse eid="AMO 5:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="AMO 5:17"/>And in all the vineyards {there will be} wailing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for I will pass through your midst,” says Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="AMO 5:18"/>Woe to the ones desiring the day of Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">What {is} this to you, the day of Yahweh?
</para>
  <para style="q1">It {is} darkness and not light.
<verse eid="AMO 5:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="AMO 5:19"/>As when a man flees from the face of the lion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the bear meets him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">or goes into  the house and rests his hand on the wall,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the snake bites him.
<verse eid="AMO 5:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="AMO 5:20"/>{Is} not the day of Yahweh darkness, and not light?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even gloom, with no brightness in it?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="AMO 5:21"/>“I hate, I reject your feasts,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will not smell  in your assemblies.
<verse eid="AMO 5:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="AMO 5:22"/>For if you offer up to me burnt offerings and your grain offerings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not accept {them};
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the peace offering of your fattened animals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not look at.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="AMO 5:23"/>Remove from me the noise of your songs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the music of your harps I will not hear.
<verse eid="AMO 5:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="AMO 5:24"/>But let justice roll down like waters,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="AMO 5:25"/>Did you bring near to me sacrifices and a grain offering
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the wilderness forty years, house of Israel?
<verse eid="AMO 5:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="AMO 5:26"/>But you carried Sikkuth your king,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Kiyyun your images, the star of your gods,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which you made for yourselves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 5:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="AMO 5:27"/>So I will exile you from farther than Damascus,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">says Yahweh, God of Armies {is} his name.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 5:27"/><verse eid="AMO 5:27"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="AMO 6"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 6:1"/>Woe to the ones at ease in Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {to} the ones trusting in the mountain of Samaria,
</para>
  <para style="q1">designated {ones} of the first of the nations
</para>
  <para style="q2">—and to them the house of Israel comes!
<verse eid="AMO 6:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 6:2"/>Cross over to Calneh and see,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and go from there to Hamath Rabbah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and go down to Gath of the Philistines.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{Are} they better than these kingdoms?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Or {is} their border greater than your border?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 6:3"/>—the ones putting far off the evil day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you bring near a seat of violence;
<verse eid="AMO 6:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 6:4"/>—the ones lying on beds of ivory,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sprawling on their couches,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and eating young rams from the flock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and calves from the midst of the stall;

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 6:5"/>—the ones improvising on the mouth of the harp;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like David they devised for themselves instruments of song;
<verse eid="AMO 6:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 6:6"/>—the ones drinking from bowls of wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they anoint {themselves} with the first of oils,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they are not grieved over the breaking of Joseph.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 6:7"/>Therefore, now they will go into exile at the head of the exiles,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the revelry of the sprawling ones will depart.
<verse eid="AMO 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 6:8"/>The Lord Yahweh has sworn by his soul—the declaration of Yahweh, the God of Armies—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I am abhorring the pride of Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his citadels I hate,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will give over a city and its fullness.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 6:9"/>And it will happen, if ten men remain in one house, then they will die.
<verse eid="AMO 6:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 6:10"/>And his kinsman and the one burning him will lift him up to bring out the bones from the house, and he will say to the one who {is} in the innermost parts of the house, “Is there yet {anyone} with you?” and he will say, “None.” Then he will say, “Hush! For not to make mention of the name of Yahweh.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 6:11"/>For, behold, Yahweh is commanding,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he will strike the great house into fragments,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the small house into fissures.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 6:12"/>Do horses run on the cliff?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Or does one plow {it} with oxen?
</para>
  <para style="q1">For you have turned justice into poisonweed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the fruit of righteousness into wormwood;
<verse eid="AMO 6:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 6:13"/>—the ones rejoicing over Lo Debar,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones saying, “Have we not by our strength taken Karnaim for ourselves?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 6:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 6:14"/>“For behold me raising up against you, house of Israel”—the declaration of Yahweh, the God of Armies—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“a nation, and they will oppress you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from Lebo Hamath to the brook of the Arabah.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 6:14"/><verse eid="AMO 6:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="AMO 7"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 7:1"/>Thus the Lord Yahweh made me see, and behold, {he} was forming a locust swarm at the beginning of the coming up of the latter growth. And behold, the latter growth {was} after the mowings of the king.
<verse eid="AMO 7:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 7:2"/>And it happened, when it had finished eating the vegetation of the land, that I said, “Lord Yahweh, please forgive! How will Jacob stand? For he {is} small.”
<verse eid="AMO 7:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 7:3"/>Yahweh relented concerning this.
“It will not be,” said Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 7:4"/>Thus the Lord Yahweh made me see, and behold, the Lord Yahweh was calling to contend by fire. And it devoured the great deep and was devouring the portion.
<verse eid="AMO 7:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 7:5"/>And I said, “Lord Yahweh, please cease! How will Jacob stand? For he {is} small.”
<verse eid="AMO 7:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 7:6"/>Yahweh relented concerning this.
“This also will not be,” said the Lord Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 7:7"/>Thus he made me see, and behold, the Lord was standing beside a wall of a plumb line, and in his hand
{was} a plumb line.
<verse eid="AMO 7:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 7:8"/>And Yahweh said to me, “What are you seeing, Amos?” And I said, “A plumb line.” And the Lord said,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Behold me placing a plumb line in the midst of my people Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not again repeat to pass over him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 7:9"/>And the high places of Isaac will be deserted,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the sanctuaries of Israel will be desolate,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will rise against the house of Jeroboam with the sword.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 7:10"/>Then Amaziah, the priest of Bethel, sent to Jeroboam, king of Israel, saying,
“Amos has conspired against you in the midst of the house of Israel. The land is not able to contain all of his words.
<verse eid="AMO 7:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 7:11"/>For thus Amos says,
‘By the sword Jeroboam will die, and Israel, going into exile, will go into exile from upon his ground.’”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 7:12"/>And Amaziah said to Amos,
“Seer, go, flee for yourself to the land of Judah, and eat bread there, and there you shall prophesy.
<verse eid="AMO 7:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 7:13"/>But {at} Bethel you shall not repeat to prophesy again, for it {is} a sanctuary of the king, and it {is} a house of a kingdom.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 7:14"/>And Amos answered and said to Amaziah, “I {am} not a prophet, and I {am} not a son of a prophet, for I {am} a herdsman, and a tender of sycamore figs.
<verse eid="AMO 7:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 7:15"/>But Yahweh took me from after the flock, and Yahweh said to me,
‘Go, prophesy to my people Israel.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 7:15"/><verse number="16" style="v" sid="AMO 7:16"/>And now, hear the word of Yahweh. You are saying,
‘You shall not prophesy against Israel, and you shall not drip against the house of Isaac.’
<verse eid="AMO 7:16"/><verse number="17" style="v" sid="AMO 7:17"/>Therefore, thus says Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">‘Your wife will prostitute herself in the city,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your sons and your daughters will fall by the sword,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and your ground will be divided by the measuring line,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you, you will die on unclean ground,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and Israel, going into exile, will go into exile from upon his ground.’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 7:17"/><verse eid="AMO 7:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="AMO 8"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 8:1"/>Thus the Lord Yahweh made me see, and behold, a basket of summer fruit!
<verse eid="AMO 8:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 8:2"/>And he said, “What are you seeing, Amos?” And I said, “A basket of summer fruit.” And Yahweh said to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“The end has come to my people Israel;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not repeat again to pass over him.
<verse eid="AMO 8:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 8:3"/>And the songs of the temple will wail in that day”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“many {are} the corpses;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in every place one has thrown {them}. Hush!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 8:4"/>Hear this, the ones trampling the needy
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to cause the afflicted of the land to cease,
<verse eid="AMO 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 8:5"/>saying, “When will the new moon pass, that we may sell grain,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the Sabbath, that we may open wheat,
</para>
  <para style="q1">to make the ephah small and to make the shekel great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to pervert balances of deceit,
<verse eid="AMO 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 8:6"/>to buy the poor with silver
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the needy in exchange for a pair of sandals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the refuse of grain we will sell?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 8:7"/>Yahweh has sworn by the pride of Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“If I ever forget all of their deeds.
<verse eid="AMO 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 8:8"/>Will not the land tremble over this,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and everyone dwelling in it mourn?
</para>
  <para style="q1">And all of it will rise like the Nile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and be cast up and sunk, like the Nile of Egypt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 8:9"/>And it will happen in that day”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q2">“that I will make the sun set at noon,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will darken the land in a day of light.
<verse eid="AMO 8:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 8:10"/>And I will turn your feasts into mourning
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of your songs into a lament.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will bring up sackcloth on all loins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and baldness on every head.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will make it like the mourning for an only child,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its end like a bitter day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 8:10"/></para>
  <para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 8:11"/>Behold, days are coming”—the declaration of the Lord Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q2">“when I will send a famine in the land,
</para>
  <para style="q1">not a famine for bread, and not a thirst for water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but rather to hear the words of Yahweh.
<verse eid="AMO 8:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 8:12"/>And they will stagger from sea to sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from the north and to the sunrise;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they will rove about to seek the word of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they will not find it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 8:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 8:13"/>In that day, the beautiful virgins will faint,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the young men, from thirst—
<verse eid="AMO 8:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 8:14"/>the ones swearing by the guilt of Samaria,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they say, ‘By the life of your god, Dan!’
</para>
  <para style="q1">and, ‘By the life of the way of Beersheba!’—
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will fall, and they will not rise again.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="AMO 8:14"/><verse eid="AMO 8:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="AMO 9"/>
  <para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="AMO 9:1"/>I saw the Lord standing by the altar, and he said,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Strike the capital so that the thresholds shake,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cut them off on the head of all of them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and their end I will kill with the sword.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A fleeing one will not flee for them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a fugitive will not escape for them.
<verse eid="AMO 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="AMO 9:2"/>If they dig into Sheol,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from there my hand will take them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And if they go up to the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from there I will bring them down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="AMO 9:3"/>And if they hide themselves in the head of Carmel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from there I will search out and take them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And if they are hidden from before my eyes in the floor of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from there I will command the serpent and it will bite them.
<verse eid="AMO 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="AMO 9:4"/>And if they go in captivity to the face of their enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from there I will command the sword and it will kill them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">And I will set my eye on them for evil
</para>
  <para style="q2">and not for good.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="AMO 9:5"/>And the Lord Yahweh of Armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the one touching the earth and it melts,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of the dwellers in it mourn,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all of it goes up like the Nile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it sinks like the Nile of Egypt;
<verse eid="AMO 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="AMO 9:6"/>the one building his stairs in the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and his vault, over the earth he founded it,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the one calling to the waters of the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he pours them out upon the face of the earth—
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh {is} his name.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="AMO 9:7"/>“Are you not like the sons of the Cushites to me, sons of Israel?”—the declaration of Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Did I not bring Israel up from the land of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the Philistines from Caphtor, and Aram from Kir?
<verse eid="AMO 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="AMO 9:8"/>Behold, the eyes of the Lord Yahweh are on the sinful kingdom,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will destroy it from upon the face of the ground.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Nevertheless, destroying, I will not destroy the house of Jacob”—the declaration of Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="AMO 9:9"/>“For behold, I am commanding,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will shake the house of Israel among all of the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as it is shaken in the sieve,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a pebble will not fall to the earth.
<verse eid="AMO 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="AMO 9:10"/>By the sword all of the sinners of my people will die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the ones saying, ‘The evil will not approach or reach as far as us.’

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="AMO 9:11"/>In that day, I will raise up the fallen booth of David,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will wall up their breaches,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will raise up his ruins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will build it as {in} the days of antiquity,
<verse eid="AMO 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="AMO 9:12"/>so that they may possess the remnant of Edom
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of the nations whom my name is called over them”—
</para>
  <para style="q2">the declaration of Yahweh, the one doing this.


<verse eid="AMO 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="AMO 9:13"/>“Behold, days are coming”—the declaration of Yahweh—
</para>
  <para style="q1">“and the plower will approach the reaper,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the treader of grapes to the sower of the seed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the mountains will drip sweet wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of the hills will melt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="AMO 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="AMO 9:14"/>And I will restore the restoration of my people Israel,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will build desolated cities and dwell {there},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they will plant vineyards and drink their wine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will make gardens and eat their fruit.
<verse eid="AMO 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="AMO 9:15"/>And I will plant them upon their ground,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will not be uprooted again from upon their ground
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I gave to them,” says Yahweh your God.
<verse eid="AMO 9:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="AMO 9"/>
</usx>
